# Binary formats: never apply end-of-line conversion.
#
# Git decides text-vs-binary by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8000
# bytes. Small PDFs often have none, so git calls them text and, on a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true, rewrites every LF as CRLF. That shifts
# every byte offset after the first newline and invalidates the xref table:
# the file still opens through lenient parsing but can no longer be written,
# which surfaced as "document is not writable" in the Windows Node smoke tests
# while Linux and macOS passed.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.p12 binary
*.pfx binary
*.cff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.crate binary
*.wasm binary

# Byte-compared text goldens: the tests assert produced == committed byte
# for byte, so a CRLF checkout fails them. Build 6 reddened the Windows
# natives leg exactly this way (serializers_over_five_documents: the goldens
# checked out CRLF under autocrlf while the serializers produce LF). eol=lf
# keeps the checkout LF on every OS; the tests keep comparing byte-for-byte
# (stripping CR there would hide a real CRLF bug in our own output). Held by
# scripts/ci/golden_dirs_check_out_lf.py, which fails a golden dir without it.
crates/pdf-engine/tests/golden/** eol=lf

# Release texts pinned to their tree bytes: fetch_models_release.py pins the
# models-v1 release's LICENSE, LICENSE-COMMERCIAL, LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt and
# MODELS-NOTICE.txt to the size and sha256 of these four tree files, and the
# release carries the LF bytes. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its
# system config, so the win-x64 release smoke checked them out CRLF and refused
# a correct release ("LICENSE is 34523 bytes, pin says 35184": 661 lines, one
# CR each). text eol=lf, not -text: the checkout stays LF on every OS, and a
# CRLF edit made on Windows is normalised to LF at commit instead of changing
# the pinned bytes. The pins and their verification stay strict. Held by
# scripts/release/test_pinned_texts_check_out_lf.py, which takes its list from
# fetch_models_release.TREE_TEXTS and proves the CRLF checkout both ways.
/LICENSE text eol=lf
/LICENSE-COMMERCIAL text eol=lf
/LICENSE-APACHE text eol=lf
/scripts/release/models-v1/MODELS-NOTICE.txt text eol=lf

# Git LFS tracking for large test corpus files
corpus/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
corpus/pdfjs/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
corpus/pdfbox/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
corpus/govdocs/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
gold-masters/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
